  "title": "Shin Saimdang",
  "summary": "Joseon-era painter, calligrapher and poet, born in 1504 and raised mainly in Gangneung by her mother and maternal grandparents, who educated her as if she were a son. She married Yi Won-su in 1522, lived at times in Hanyang, Paju and Pyeongchang, and often returned to Gangneung. She died in 1551; her son Yi I became a noted Confucian scholar.",
